WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:05.700
In 1964, a series of race riots between Chinese

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.280
and Malays broke out in Singapore,

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.040
leaving dozens dead and hundreds injured.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.260
When it came to racial riots, it was just madness.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.640
I experienced myself firsthand.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.620
And that was when I felt so threatened

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.880
and where I was almost killed.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.900
Communal tensions that led to the 1964 race riots

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.340
contributed to Singapore’s separation

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.900
from Malaysia the next year.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.580
To avoid the mistakes of the past, Singapore’s founding

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.740
Prime Minister Lee Kuan Yew and his team aimed to

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.420
create a society where different races, religions

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.580
and cultures could live peacefully.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.980
Here is how Singapore built a fairly harmonious society.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.000
Singapore has a population of 5.7 million people.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.360
Among the 3.5 million who are citizens,

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.820
76% percent are Chinese

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.340
and 15% are Malay.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.660
Malays are the native people of the island.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:10.840
During the British colonialism,

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.160
immigrants from China, India

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.440
and other parts of the world came to Singapore

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.360
as the island was being developed into a trading port.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.620
By the 1870s, Chinese had become

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.300
the majority population in Singapore.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.680
In 1959, Singapore obtained

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.000
self-governance from the British.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.580
To completely break away from colonial rule,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.140
in 1963, Singapore joined the Federation of Malaya,

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.380
part of Malaysia today.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.760
But it was a difficult union plagued with differences

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.540
in political approach, economic conditions

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.540
and sharp exchanges between leaders from both sides.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.620
The relationship then was just not getting on,

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.300
between the majority Singapore Chinese,

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.680
75 percent Chinese from Singapore,

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.760
in a merger with Malaysia,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.580
which are predominantly Malay,

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.180
55, 60 percent Malays.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.360
The community in Singapore, the majority Chinese

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.640
had been doing very well economically.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.240
The Malaysians felt that they would be undermined,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.320
should the Chinese in Singapore continued to

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:18.160
gain economic supremacy over the peninsula.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.180
And in Singapore, the idea was that

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.560
all races should be treated equally.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.480
But in Malaysia, that was a different outlook

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.460
because Malay leaders and Malay politicians felt

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.400
they were sons of the soil.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.200
There was a sense that Malays should always

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.540
have the political dominant position.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.420
In 1964, increasing racial tensions between Malays

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.700
and Chinese led to a series of riots.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.700
Singaporean Malays are predominantly Muslims.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.200
On July 21, a Muslim holiday to celebrate

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:55.880
the Prophet Muhammad’s birthday,

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.620
clashes broke out between Malay participants

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.580
and Chinese bystanders during a procession.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.020
Violence spread across the island,

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.300
ravaging Singapore for weeks,

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:10.560
leaving 23 dead and 454 injured.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.080
In September, another series of riots triggered

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.860
by the killing of a Malay rickshaw rider broke out.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.800
Zainul and a few friends were on their way back home

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.400
from Friday Prayers when the curfew

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.620
was imposed on September 2.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.400
Buses were full, so they jumped on a lorry for a ride.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.240
But the lorry broke down in a Chinese area.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.600
A lot of Chinese youngsters were standing

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.300
by the roadside watching.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.740
And suddenly when they saw this group of

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.000
about 20 Malays

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.540
rising from the lorry to come down

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.560
to get alternative transport,

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.360
they must have thought that

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.080
we were there to attack them.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.160
And the next second,

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.900
they came out with bicycle chains,

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.940
iron rods, acid bombs

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.360
and pandemonium broke loose.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.400
They just randomly were hammering,

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.120
killing people on the street.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.840
But fortunately for me,

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.940
I was able to grab a moving taxi

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.880
and fled to safety.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.880
But that wasn't the end of the story.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.080
When I took the taxi ride and reached the other side

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.780
where I live,

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.560
which is Geylang area, which is the Malay area.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:22.800
It was the reverse.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.500
Malays were beating up

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:27.340
innocent Chinese,

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.820
trishaw pullers, fruit sellers

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.200
who used to be friends at one time.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.040
The September riots resulted in 13 deaths

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.620
and left another 106 injured.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.500
About a year later,

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.520
Singapore separated from Malaysia

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.540
and became an independent state.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.920
Be firm, be calm.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.340
We are going to have a multi-racial nation

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:52.980
in Singapore.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.480
We will set the example.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.240
This is not a Malay nation;

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.740
this is not a Chinese nation;

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.540
this is not an Indian nation.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.380
Everybody will have his place:

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.220
equal;

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.260
language, culture, religion.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.900
The Singaporean government enshrined multiracialism

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.840
in its constitution and implemented major policies

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.620
and initiatives based on these principles,

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.060
for education, housing, politics

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.700
and community development.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.240
One of the first things that Singapore’s leaders did

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.660
was to break down the language barrier

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.660
between ethnic groups.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:31.960
Four official languages English, Chinese,

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.720
Malay and Tamil

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.880
were established,

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.660
but English was designated as a common language.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.980
People in Singapore are required to take English

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.060
as a first language

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.240
as well as a mother tongue language.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.080
So that enables them to not just

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.800
hold on to their heritage, their ethnic culture,

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.300
but at the same time be able to interact

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.300
with people of a different race.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.400
At first, there was resistance from Chinese parents.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.200
But, enrollments to Chinese schools gradually dwindled

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.600
and those to English schools grew.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.400
English is the language of the civil service,

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:08.840
of the government.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.180
Parents saw the writing on the wall.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.580
If English is the language of the civil service,

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.200
you go to an English school,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.160
so that your child can get a job in the civil service,

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.080
which is an iron rice bowl.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.580
English became in a way

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.460
a unifying language for Singapore.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.040
And it was a very important decision

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.240
because that makes Singapore so relevant in the world

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:34.240
and gave us our position.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:37.840
Racial segregation dating back to

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.340
the British colonial rule

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.060
was thought to be one of the reasons for the race riots.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.700
So in the 1960s and 1970s,

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.500
the Singaporean government forcibly

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:49.100
removed people from racial enclaves

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:53.440
and relocated all races to new public housing estates,

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.000
where about 80% of Singaporean households live today.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:59.380
Well over 400,000 people,

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.400
a quarter of Singapore’s population

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.600
has been rehoused in the last five years,

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.820
in these bright, modern, airy flats.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:08.140
Nowhere in the world, except in Russia...

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:10.300
Despite the government’s early efforts,

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:13.140
by the 1980s, racial enclaves were forming

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.140
within the public housing estates.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:19.640
In 1989, the Ethnic Integration Policy was introduced

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:22.020
to ensure a mix of Chinese, Indians

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:25.020
and Malays in each public housing block.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:28.460
It's not just having different race groups

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.640
on the same corridor and they walk down the corridor

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.120
and say hello to each other.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.720
Or they meet in the town square

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:38.020
and they see different race groups.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.960
Their children go to the same neighborhood school.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.220
And that is the value.

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.720
But critics see mixing ethnic groups

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.700
in public housing as a way of social control.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.940
On a political level, Singapore has policies

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.880
to ensure multiracial representation.

00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:01.260
In 1988, an amendment to the Parliamentary Elections Act was passed.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:05.120
This introduced the Group Representation Constituency,

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.860
or the GRC which required political parties

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.360
to field at least one minority candidate

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:16.060
in each GRC team composed of 3 to 6 members.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.200
Currently, there are 17 GRCs,

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.800
which means there are at least 17 minority members

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.620
among the total 93 members of the parliament.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:28.400
Previously you could have a party putting up

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:31.480
a Chinese candidate just hoping to get the majority

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:32.740
Chinese to vote for them

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:35.160
without having to worry about the Malay voters.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:38.540
But now no party, no candidate

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.820
can behave in that way anymore.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:45.220
But detractors said Group Representation Constituency

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.440
was introduced to make it harder

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.900
for the opposition to win elections.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:53.640
In 2016, the Constitution of Singapore was revised

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:56.080
to include 'reserved elections'.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.800
This meant that a presidential election would be

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.900
reserved for a particular racial group if no one

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.080
from that community had been President

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.720
for the past 30 years.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.340
The 2017 election was the first reserved election

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:13.020
and it was reserved for the Malay community.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.940
But compared with the Prime Minister of Singapore,

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.540
the President plays a largely ceremonial role

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.440
and doesn't hold much power.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:26.600
The government also initiated ethnicity-based

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.900
self-help groups to uplift the socio-economic status

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:30.800
of the poor.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.380
Employees in Singapore are expected to contribute

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.920
a small percentage of their monthly income

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.120
to one of the four ethnic self-help group funds

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:42.160
according to their ethnicity.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.400
These funds are mainly used to subsidize tuition

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:48.520
and help upgrade skills for lower-income groups.

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:52.120
But ethnicity-based self-help groups

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:55.240
were criticized for emphasizing the issue of race.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.340
In recent years, four different self-help groups

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.420
started to run joint programs.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.500
So I wouldn't say that Singapore's

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.180
racial relation is perfect,

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.200
but definitely we have come a long way

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:12.360
since the 1960s.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.100
For multiculturalism, multiracialism to succeed,

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.380
there has to be a visible hand in society.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:21.100
I think we've done quite well.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:26.480
We have not had an inter-racial riot since 1969.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.880
Singapore is a stable society

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.360
and it is this stability

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:34.360
that has helped us develop economically.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:39.980
Singapore has strict anti-racism and anti-rioting laws.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:43.100
The absence of race riots doesn’t mean there are no

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.880
racial tensions and racial disparities.

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.740
Today, Singapore faces challenges to shrink

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.960
the income gap between Malays

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.400
and other ethnic groups.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:53.920
Among the minorities

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.300
that feel that they are marginalized,

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.360
they couldn't speak all of it

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:00.700
because the whole system is structured

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.280
in such a way that it should be legitimate

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.960
that the reason why you are where you are

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.740
is because you haven't done well.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.420
Whereas if you dive further

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.760
and look at some of the structural issues,

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:16.460
you realize that the reason why they are not doing well,

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:17.460
certain racial groups are not doing well,

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.320
maybe because there are certain structural issues

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:23.400
and challenges that we have not been able to address

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:24.760
in the last 50 years.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:26.940
Be there in the education sector,

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:27.880
be there in the housing market,

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:29.560
be there in the employment sector.

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:33.520
All these concerns about income,

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:37.740
the lack of mobility will intersect with racial identity.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:39.120
And in the long run,

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:42.960
this could generate a perpetual cycle of unhappiness,

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:43.700
of discontent.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:48.020
Overt racism might have been reduced in Singapore,

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:51.240
but covert discrimination still exists.

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:55.240
Researchers found that over half of Malays and Indians

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:58.540
in Singapore perceived discriminatory treatment at work.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:02.540
Recently, coronavirus outbreaks in cramped dorms

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.000
where many South Asian migrant workers live

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:08.000
has also highlighted the inequalities that still exist

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.620
in different parts of Singapore's society.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:17.280
The maintenance of racial harmony

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:19.760
is a work in progress.

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:22.940
The goalposts change all the time,

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:24.480
and you've got to keep catching up.

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.980
But what hasn’t changed is that Racial Harmony Day

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:31.640
is celebrated on July 21st each year in Singapore

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.260
to commemorate the 1964 race riots,

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.540
and remind Singaporeans that racial harmony

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.280
shouldn’t be taken for granted.

